# Files this tree's own build GENERATES.
#
# OpenSSL's release tarball, unlike git, ships no .gitignore, and this port is
# configured and built IN PLACE with the tree tracked -- so every file its
# Makefile derives from a tracked .in/.pl source turns up as untracked noise
# after a build.  The list below is exactly the Makefile's GENERATED,
# GENERATED_MANDATORY and GENERATED_PODS variables, which is also precisely
# what `make distclean` removes here.
#
# Listed one per line rather than globbed: most of these sit in directories
# full of REAL sources of the same extension (include/openssl holds 41
# generated headers alongside dozens of shipped ones), so a pattern wide enough
# to catch them would hide tracked sources too.
#
# Regenerate after changing OpenSSL version:
#   sed -n '/^GENERATED[A-Z_]*=/,/^[A-Za-z_]*=/p' Makefile   (see repo root .gitignore)

